  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating Ge/ZnS multilayer filter on CaF2 substrate under normal incidence from air ambient. Layer sequence: Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS-Ge-ZnS (24 finite layers total). Initialize all Ge layers at 550 nm with optimization bounds [467.5, 632.5] nm. Initialize all ZnS layers at 900 nm with optimization bounds [765, 1035] nm. Use coherent TMM solver across wavelength range 3600-5200 nm. Optimize for four objectives: maximize mean transmittance in 4150-4350 nm band, maximize mean transmittance in 4550-4750 nm band, minimize mean transmittance in 3600-4000 nm band, minimize mean transmittance in 4850-5200 nm band. Use interior-point or trust-region optimizer that penalizes large inter-layer thickness ratios. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3600-4000 nm, 4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm, 4850-5200 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um bands; low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance in stopbands; high reflectance in passbands. manufacturing constraints: no metal layers; maximum 24 layers; conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating Ge/ZnS dielectric filter on CaF2 from air at normal incidence. Maximize mean transmittance in 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm bands while minimizing mean transmittance in 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm bands using coherent TMM over 3600-5200 nm. Layer counts and bounds are fixed; optimize all 24 thicknesses within provided ranges.",
